      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** Adding `arch_pre_system_jump()` immediately after `chip_pre_system_jump()` in `jump_to_image()` (`common/system.c`) and migrating RISC-V PMP and FPMCU sysjump teardown out of `HOOK_SYSJUMP` ensures that memory protection and peripheral teardown remain after `interrupt_disable_all()` when `HOOK_SYSJUMP` is moved back before `interrupt_disable_all()` in https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/8634174 (resolving both b/519694070 and b/575868788). However, in this CL (`8634173`), `zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` and `zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c` call `arm_core_mpu_disable()` inside `chip_pre_system_jump()`—which contradicts the new contract documented in `include/system.h` (lines 797–800) that `chip_pre_system_jump()` tears down peripherals and stops the system clock *\"while CPU memory protection is still active\"*, and causes `bloonchipper` to disable the ARM MPU *before* `sys_clock_disable()`.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Separating `chip_pre_system_jump()` (SoC/program peripheral and clock teardown with CPU memory protection active) from `arch_pre_system_jump()` (CPU core MPU/PMP teardown immediately prior to jumping) is a clean two-phase design. However, the relation chain (`8634173` -\u003e `8634174` -\u003e `8633417` -\u003e `8635773`) introduces avoidable churn: this CL moves `helipilot`\u0027s `prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec()` (which *only* calls `arm_core_mpu_disable()`) and `bloonchipper`\u0027s `arm_core_mpu_disable()` into `chip_pre_system_jump()`, only for https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/8635773 at the top of the stack to delete `chip_pre_system_jump()` from `helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c` and move `arm_core_mpu_disable()` into `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c`\u0027s `arch_pre_system_jump()`. Moving `arm_core_mpu_disable()` directly to `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c` before (or as part of) migrating `HOOK_SYSJUMP` avoids touching `helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c` twice and preserves the `include/system.h` invariant at every commit in the stack.\n* **Code Simplicity:** `zephyr/test/fpmcu/tests/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` (line 9) retains an unused `#include \"hooks.h\"` after `prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec` was converted from `DECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_SYSJUMP, ...)` to `chip_pre_system_jump()`. In `zephyr/fake/system_fake.c` (lines 18–33), `ztest_interrupt_disable_all()` discards the lock key returned by `irq_lock()` and `system_jump_to_booter()` calls `irq_unlock(0)` with a hardcoded `0` key instead of saving and restoring the key from `irq_lock()`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Function signatures, `__overridable` / `__override` annotations, and Doxygen comments in `include/system.h` and `common/system.c` follow ChromiumOS EC and Zephyr conventions.\n* **Security:** Ensuring PMP (`z_riscv_pmp_clear_all()`) and MPU (`arm_core_mpu_disable()`) teardown only execute after interrupts are globally disabled in `jump_to_image()` prevents an interrupt-driven host command (such as `EC_CMD_FLASH_READ`) from preempting sysjump teardown while rollback flash protection is unlocked (b/519694070). Maintaining active MPU protection during `chip_pre_system_jump()` (by not calling `arm_core_mpu_disable()` prior to peripheral/clock teardown in `bloonchipper`) further hardens the pre-jump teardown window.\n* **Testing:**\n  1. `zephyr/test/fpmcu/tests/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` (`test_chip_pre_system_jump`, lines 55–64) only checks `stm32_reset_line_toggle_fake.call_count \u003d\u003d 1` and `arm_core_mpu_disable_fake.call_count \u003d\u003d 1`. Unlike `test_tim2` directly above it, it does not verify the reset controller device or reset bit passed in `arg0_history[0]` / `arg1_history[0]`, nor does it verify that `sys_clock_disable()` was called.\n  2. `zephyr/test/jump_data/src/main.c` (`test_pre_system_jump_defaults`, lines 504–508) calls `chip_pre_system_jump()` and `arch_pre_system_jump()` with zero assertions.\n  3. Neither `zephyr/shim/core/riscv/mpu.c` (`arch_pre_system_jump()` calling `z_riscv_pmp_clear_all()`) nor `zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c` has unit test coverage for its pre-sysjump callback.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** At `Size: M (+100, -47)` across 10 files, this CL bundles three independently revertible concerns across common system infrastructure, test fakes, RISC-V architecture shim, and FPMCU board programs (and the ChromiumOS EC project guidelines require splitting shared/common code changes from board-specific changes):\n  1. **CL 1 (Test Fake Refactoring)**: Replace `system_fake_is_interrupt_disabled()` / `system_fake_reset_interrupt_disabled()` in `zephyr/fake/system_fake.c` and `zephyr/fake/include/system_fake.h` with `irq_lock()` / `irq_unlock()` and `arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled()` in `zephyr/test/jump_tags/src/jump_tags.c`.\n  2. **CL 2 (Core System API \u0026 Architecture Shims)**: Introduce `arch_pre_system_jump()` in `include/system.h` and `common/system.c` with unit tests in `zephyr/test/jump_tags/src/jump_tags.c` and `zephyr/test/jump_data/src/main.c`, and migrate `zephyr/shim/core/riscv/mpu.c` (and `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c` from https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/8635773) to `arch_pre_system_jump()`.\n  3. **CL 3 (FPMCU Board Teardown Migration)**: Migrate `zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` and `zephyr/test/fpmcu/tests/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` peripheral/clock teardown out of `HOOK_SYSJUMP` into `chip_pre_system_jump()` (and remove the redundant MPU hook from `zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c`).\n* **Commit Message:**\n  1. **Factual inaccuracy in body**: Paragraph 2 claims *\"Move STM32 timers, UARTs, and Cortex-M Systick teardown in bloonchipper and helipilot to chip_pre_system_jump().\"* `helipilot` is a Nuvoton NPCX797FC board (not STM32) and does not touch STM32 timers, UARTs, or SysTick in `zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/src/ec_quirks.c`—it only calls `arm_core_mpu_disable()`. Conversely, the body omits mentioning that `arm_core_mpu_disable()` in `bloonchipper` and `helipilot` is moved to `chip_pre_system_jump()`.\n  2. **Undocumented change in body**: The commit message does not mention removing `system_fake_is_interrupt_disabled()` and `system_fake_reset_interrupt_disabled()` from `zephyr/fake/include/system_fake.h` and `zephyr/fake/system_fake.c` in favor of `irq_lock()` / `irq_unlock()` and `arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled()`.",
